8. Transition Model

Each transition SHALL define:

Property	Description
Source State	Current state
Target State	Next state
Transition Trigger	Reason for change
Authorized Roles	Who may execute
Preconditions	Required conditions
Postconditions	Expected outcome

Unauthorized transitions SHALL be rejected.

9. Lifecycle Governance

Each lifecycle transition SHALL record:

Transition ID
Timestamp
Initiator
Approver
Justification
Policies evaluated
Audit references

Governance SHALL accompany every transition.

10. Quality Gates

Lifecycle progression MAY require quality gates.

Examples include:

Transition	Example Quality Gate
Draft → Validated	Schema validation
Validated → Reviewed	Technical review
Reviewed → Approved	Governance approval
Approved → Published	Release authorization
Published → Active	Operational verification

Quality gates SHALL be explicitly defined.

11. Lifecycle Inheritance

Every specialization of the Canonical Atlas Object SHALL inherit the Canonical Lifecycle Model.

Canonical Atlas Object
        │
        ▼
Lifecycle Model
        │
 ┌──────┼─────────────┐
 ▼      ▼             ▼
CEA     DR           CEV
 │       │            │
 ▼       ▼            ▼
Inherited Lifecycle

Specializations MAY introduce additional states but SHALL preserve canonical lifecycle semantics.

12. Lifecycle Events

Lifecycle transitions MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples:

Object Published
Object Approved
Object Archived
Object Retired

Lifecycle events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

13. Preservation

Retired objects SHALL:

Preserve identity.
Preserve version history.
Preserve provenance.
Preserve relationships.
Preserve audit records.

Retirement SHALL NOT remove traceability.

14. Quality Requirements

Every lifecycle implementation SHALL ensure:

Completeness
Consistency
Auditability
Governance compliance
Traceability
Recoverability
Historical integrity
Operational clarity
15. Conformance

A lifecycle implementation conforms if it:

Implements canonical lifecycle states.
Supports governed transitions.
Preserves lifecycle history.
Records transition provenance.
Implements quality gates.
Supports lifecycle inheritance.
16. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Adaptive lifecycle profiles.
Domain-specific lifecycle extensions.
AI-assisted lifecycle governance.
Cross-enterprise lifecycle federation.
Automated policy evaluation.
Self-governing lifecycle workflows.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical lifecycle semantics.

